	(text "INPUT PROTECTION (record section 3). Self-acting: nothing here depends on firmware or on a rail it protects.\nF1: Nano2 453 15 A (65 V DC) soldered, first in the path: dead-short backstop; the GST360A36's hiccup protection acts first on its own supply (SPEC ruling). No polyfuse.\nJobs: reverse polarity, reverse-current blocking (required so the regen clamp can sit at ~45 V, section 5), inrush, overcurrent.\nU1 LTC4364IS-1 (SO-16): surge stopper + ideal diode in one part. LATCH-OFF (-1, operator ruling 2026-09-22): a fault kills every rail, MCU included,\nso D6 is powered from VIN_RAW and lit by FLT: the fault shows with the board dark. Power-cycle clears it. TODO(detailing): confirm FLT pin's voltage rating vs VIN.\nTODO(detailing): wire Q1/Q2/R1 per LTC4364 datasheet Figure 1; Q1 chosen off its pulse SOA curve (1000 uF at 36 V = ~0.65 J in linear region).\nR2 is the INA228 shunt: Kelvin taps INA_SENSE_P (BUS_PROT side) and INA_SENSE_N (+BUS side) route as a tight pair to the Sensing sheet.\nBulk: C1/C2 polymer mirrored about the stamp centerline (SPEC ruling), C3/C4 MLCC for HF. Decoupling only; caps do nothing for regen."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 150 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2377f9a8-4619-466c-8d16-4a87c9753471")
	)
